ng":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Kyverna Therapeutics, Inc., a late-stage biopharmaceutical company, focuses on developing cell therapies for patients with autoimmune diseases. Its lead product candidate is KYV-101, an autologous CD19 CAR T-cell product candidate for the treatment of stiff person syndrome, myasthenia gravis, and autoimmune diseases. The company is also developing KYV-102, an autologous CD19 CAR T-cell product candidate with whole blood rapid manufacturing; and KYV-201, an allogeneic CD19 CAR T-cell product candidate. It has a license and collaboration agreement with Intellia Therapeutics, Inc. to research and develop an allogeneic CD19-directed CAR cell therapy product. The company was formerly known as BAIT Therapeutics, Inc. and changed its name to Kyverna Therapeutics, Inc. in October 2019. Kyverna Therapeutics, Inc. was incorporated in 2018 and is headquartered in Emeryville, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Warner  Biddle | CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 149 people. Stock-based compensation of $68K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Kyverna Therapeutics, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $312M market cap.","The company is burning through $154M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -347.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 5.4% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 7.0% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (17.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 106% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Large open-market insider purchases (net $1.7M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Kyverna Therapeutics, Inc. (NASDAQ:KYTX) Stock Now Rated \u201cModerate Buy\u201d by Wall Street Brokerages","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/02/kyverna-therapeutics-inc-nasdaqkytx-stock-now-rated-moderate-buy-by-wall-street-brokerages.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793611850.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.765,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Kyverna Therapeutics (NASDAQ:KYTX) Stock Falls 2.2% \u2013 Time to Sell?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/28/kyverna-therapeutics-nasdaqkytx-